   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the election law, in relation to early voting polling places\nfor certain special, primary and run-off primary elections at which no voters\nare eligible to vote",
    "basePrintNo": "S6215",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6215-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §8-600, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6215\n\nSPONSOR: BRESLIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to early voting polling\nplaces for certain special, primary and run-off primary elections at\nwhich no voters are eligible to vote\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nAuthorizes a change of location of early voting polling places for\ncertain special, primary and run-off primary elections.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\n§ 1-Amends subdivision 2 of § 8-600 of the Election Law by re-lettering\nparagraphs (b), (c) and (d) and adding a new paragraph (b) to state\nthat, \"For any special, primary or run-off primary election at which no\nvoters of the municipality with the highest population within the county\nare eligible to vote, the board of elections may, in lieu of having an\nearly voting polling place in such municipality, designate a polling\nplace for early voting in the municipality with the highest population\nwithin the county within which the voters are eligible to vote at such\nspecial, primary, or run-off primary election.\"\n\n§ 2-Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAt primary, special or run-off primary elections, the situation often\narises whereby not all municipalities within a county have an election.\nIf the municipality with the largest population has no contest and its\nvoters are ineligible to participate in the primary, it is imprudent to\nrequire an early voting location to be in such municipality where no one\ncan vote.  This legislation would relieve a board of elections of the\nrequirement to put an early voting site in a municipality that is not\nparticipating in a primary or special election, provided that, in lieu\nof that, an early voting site is placed in a municipality with the high-\nest population within the county where voters are eligible to vote at\nsuch primary or special election.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
